    "text": "To determine how much the developer should sell each lot for to break even, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the land.\n2. Determine the total revenue needed to break even.\n3. Divide the total revenue needed by the number of lots to find the price per lot.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the land.**\n\nThe developer bought 4 acres at $1,863 per acre. So, the total cost is:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ acres} \\times \\$1,863 \\text{ per acre} = \\$7,452 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total revenue needed to break even.**\n\nTo break even, the total revenue from selling the 9 lots must equal the total cost of the land. So, the total revenue needed is:\n\\[ \\$7,452 \\]\n\n**Step 3: Divide the total revenue needed by the number of lots to find the price per lot.**\n\nThe price per lot is:\n\\[ \\frac{\\$7,452}{9 \\text{ lots}} = \\$828 \\text{ per lot} \\]\n\nTherefore, the developer should sell each lot for \\(\\boxed{828}\\) to break even.",
